ox1505","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/greenfox1505/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/greenfox1505/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/greenfox1505/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/greenfox1505/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/greenfox1505/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/greenfox1505/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/greenfox1505/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/greenfox1505/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/greenfox1505/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-13T22:48:50Z","updated_at":"2026-04-13T22:48:50Z","body":"> Needs a proposal.\r\n\r\nYeah, my mistake, I forgot to link the proposal\r\n\r\n> That's not a feature, trying to get UID from built-in resources will result in errors.\r\n\r\nYeah, it seems to just return the \"file path\" which is something like `res://some_scene.tres::Resource_bnu62`. Which, I would maybe argue is an issue with `ResourceUID::path_to_uid(` quietly not indicating a failure to resolve and returning the original string. IMHO, that should maybe indicate failure in some way or be renamed to indicate that it does not.\r\n\r\nBut if the preference here is to leave this field blank on embedded resources, that can be done without changes to `ResourceUID`.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4240107048/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]